// The check `@foreignEntry` exists for. A module `static` is one object PER THREAD (`KAMA_ISOLATE_LOCAL`
// is `_Thread_local`), so a callback running on a thread kama did not create — an audio render callback,
// a completion port — sees `gain` as its declared initialiser, 0, never the 7 that `setup` assigned on
// the main isolate. That program compiles, runs, and mixes silence. The region declared by `@foreignEntry`
// makes it a compile error: a read of a static that is assigned anywhere outside the region can only ever
// see the initialiser. (PROBED: compiled clean on 0.9.158.)
static int32 gain = 0;
fn void setup() { gain = 7; }
@foreignEntry fn void render(int32 frames) {
    int32 g = gain;   // ERROR: `setup` assigns `gain` outside the region
}
fn int32 main() { setup(); return 0; }
